 "title": "Grain | Maple River Grain &amp; Agronomy, LLC - Maple River Coop - MRGA",
 "text": "Grain | Maple River Grain & Agronomy, LLC - Maple River Coop - MRGA\nMain\nUtilities\nGrain\nCash Bids\nGrain Programs\nGrain Discounts\nTrucking Rates\nWeather\nAgronomy\nCasselton Fert Plant\nCrop Protection\nPrecision Ag\nProfitability Calculator\nSeed & Seed Treatment\nMeet Our Team\nFinance\nApplications\nNews\nAgricultural News\nEvents\nNewsletter Archive\nAbout Us\nBoard Of Directors\nCommunities\nScholarships\nPatronage Rates\nOur History\nPhotoContest\nLocations\nContact Us\nCareers\nPortal Login\nLocations\nContact Us\nCareers\nPortal Login\nGrain\nWe offer a variety of grain marketing options tailored to fit your farm.\nCash Bids\nGrain Programs\nGrain Discounts\nGrain Overview\nThe Casselton Shuttle Facility was completed in 2005 and is among the finest in the Upper Midwest. We have built additional storage in 2010, 2014 and 2016. The current licensed storage capacity at our Casselton Terminal is 9.6 million bushels. Our grain receiving capacity is 75,000 bushels per hour, and we can unload 450 trucks a day.\nWe also offer automated truck processing, which speeds up deliveries while triple-ensuring the identity and weight of every load we receive. Incoming deliveries of corn, soybeans and wheat are processed by North Dakota Grain Inspection for official weights and grades. North Dakota Grain Inspection is a federally designated laboratory licensed to officially sample and grade grain under the United States Grain Standards Act\nFor additional information, or to learn more about delivery, storage or grain marketing options, contact the grain team in Casselton or at any of our other grain facilities.\nGrain Contacts >\nGrain Hours\nCasselton Office Hours\nMon - Friday 8:00AM - 4:30PM\nCasselton Grain Receiving Hours\nMon-Friday 8:00AM - 5:00PM\nSaturday & Sunday Call\nFor outside locations receiving hours please call.\nContact Information\nToll Free: 800-568-5402\nPhone: 701-347-4465\nCash Bids\n&cols=name%2Ccash%2Cbasis%2Cchange%2Cprice%2Cmonth&colNames=name%3ADELIVERY+PERIOD%2Cmonth%3ASYMBOL%2Cprice%3AFUTURES+PRICE%2Cbasis%3ABASIS%2Ccash%3ACASH%2Cchange%3ACHANGE&hideRows=true\" width=\"100%\" height=\"800px\" style=\"border: none;\">\nMarket News & Commentary\nGrain Programs\nThere are plenty of buyers out there who would be happy to take grain off your hands at the lowest possible price. But at MRGA, we don’t think that way. Our customers are also our owners, and it’s important to us that they make money, too. So we do everything we can to help our farmer-members price their grain profitably, whether that means selling right out of the field in the fall, storing it and waiting for a higher price later on, or pricing ahead for delivery on the futures market. If you’d like a free, comprehensive evaluation of your grain marketing options, please call the grain division team at our Casselton office to set up an appointment.\nClick to download PDF documents:\n2026 Corn Price Later\n2026 Soybean Price Later\n2026 Wheat Price Later\nQuestions for our Grain Merchandisers? Login to send a message or call your rep.\nPortal Login\nGrain Premium & Discounts\nIt was a late spring and an early fall, which is a bad combination for grain coming out of the field. Fortunately, our high capacity drying equipment is ready to run around the clock. With nearly 10 million bushels of storage capacity, we will do everything we can to dry corn, wheat and soybeans, to store it until you are ready to sell.\nClick to download PDF documents:\nWheat Discounts\nCorn FM and TW\nSB Shrink and Drying\nCorn Shrink and Drying\nGrain Contacts\nClick photos for more info:\nAlex Richard\nCEO\nKim Bender\nMerchandiser\nTanner McDaniel\nGrain Merchandiser\nDarren Bjornson\nGrain Merchandiser\nJoe Eberhardt\nDispatch/Custom Hauling\nSign up for our Newsletter:\n*First Name:\n*Last Name:\n*Email:\nGrain/Agronomy Notifications:\nPlease Select One\nGrain\nAgronomy\nGrain/Agronomy\nSales Person:\nSelect Agronomy Sales Person\nKarl Berg\nJon Ellingson\nMike Weed\nSecurity code:\nHeadquarters\n1850 Governors Drive\nCasselton, ND 58012\n701-347-4465\nAGRONOMY\nGRAIN\nABOUT US\nFINANCE\nNEWS\nLOCATIONS\nCAREERS\nCONTACT US\nPrivacy & Terms of Service\n|\nSite Map\n© Maple River Coop - All rights reserved\nSearch for:\nMinimum 3 character allowed.\nAlex Richard\nCEO\nExt. 1007\n×\nKim Bender\nMerchandiser\nOffice: (701) 347-3129\nExt: 1008\nDirect: 701.347.3129\n×\nTanner McDaniel\nGrain Merchandiser\nOffice: (701) 347-3138\nExt: 1018\nDirect: 701.347.3138\n×\nDarren Bjornson\nGrain Merchandiser\nOffice: (218) 979-4167\nExt: 2044\nDirect: 218-979-4167\n×\nJoe Eberhardt\nDispatch/Custom Hauling\nExtension 1051\n×",
